1. Executive Summary
The proposed platform is an agricultural consulting and marketplace website that connects farmers, trained agricultural professionals, farms seeking investment, individual investors, organisations, and the platform administrator. It will help users discover expertise, request and deliver agricultural services, collaborate on projects, review eligible farm investment opportunities, make or receive payments through approved payment channels, and monitor project or investment progress through structured reports.
The platform should be built as a secure, mobile-friendly web application with role-based registration, profiles, dashboards, workflows, notifications, and an administrative back office. The first release should prioritise trust, verification, transparent project reporting, and a clear separation between service payments and investment funds.
2. Product Vision and Objectives
Vision: Build a trusted digital hub that makes agricultural expertise, collaboration, and responsible farm-development opportunities easier to access.
• Connect farmers with verified and appropriately skilled agricultural professionals.
• Enable organisations to discover the platform and collaborate with the organisation on agricultural projects.
• Allow farms to create profiles and submit project or investment proposals for review.
• Provide individuals with access to reviewed farm opportunities and transparent progress updates.
• Support secure payment collection for platform-approved services and project-related transactions.
• Give farmers, partners, and investors a clear view of milestones, deliverables, evidence, and reported progress.
• Create a scalable foundation for future marketplace, reporting, and project-management features.
3. Scope
3.1 In scope for the initial release (MVP)
• Public website pages explaining the organisation, services, collaboration model, and how the platform works.
• Registration, login, password reset, role selection, and user profile management.
• Farmer and farm registration, profile completion, and document submission.
• Agricultural professional registration, skills profiles, experience, location, service categories, and verification status.
• Service directory and basic search/filtering for professionals.
• Service request or hiring workflow between farmers and professionals.
• Organisation/partner enquiry and collaboration project intake.
• Farm opportunity submission, review, approval/rejection, and investor-facing opportunity pages.
• Investor registration and profile, subject to applicable identity and compliance checks.
• Payment gateway integration for approved transactions; payment records and transaction status.
• Project/investment progress reports, milestones, supporting evidence, and investor/partner dashboard views.
• Notifications by email and in-platform alerts; SMS/WhatsApp can be added if budget and integrations permit.
• Admin dashboard for users, farms, professionals, organisations, opportunities, payments, reports, and disputes.
• Audit logs and basic platform analytics.
3.2 Out of scope unless separately approved
• Automated investment advice, guaranteed returns, or a promise that any farm opportunity will be profitable.
• Operating as a bank, custodian, securities exchange, fund manager, or escrow provider without the required approvals and partner arrangements.
• A full accounting/ERP system for farms.
• Native iOS and Android apps; the MVP should be responsive on mobile browsers.
• Automated credit scoring, lending, insurance underwriting, or complex secondary trading of investments.
• IoT sensors or automatic farm telemetry; reports may be manually submitted in the MVP.
