5. Core User Journeys
5.1 Farmer hires a professional
1. Farmer creates an account and verifies their email/phone.
2. Farmer completes their profile, farm location, production type, needs, and preferred contact method.
3. Farmer searches or browses verified professionals by expertise, location, service, availability, and profile information.
4. Farmer submits a service request describing the task, location, timeline, and budget where applicable.
5. Professional accepts, declines, or requests clarification; the farmer can compare responses.
6. The parties agree on scope, deliverables, timeline, and payment terms.
7. Payment is processed through an approved gateway or partner flow where applicable.
8. Professional updates status and submits deliverables; farmer confirms completion or raises an issue.
9. Both parties can rate the experience after completion, subject to moderation.
5.2 Farm submits an investment opportunity
10. Farm owner registers and completes a farm profile.
11. Farm owner submits the opportunity description, use of funds, proposed structure, financial assumptions, risks, timeline, evidence, and required documents.
12. Admin and designated compliance reviewers check completeness, authenticity, disclosures, and eligibility.
13. The opportunity is approved, returned for edits, or rejected. Only approved opportunities appear publicly.
14. Eligible users view the opportunity page, supporting documents, risks, and status.
15. If enabled by legal/compliance approval, an investor completes required checks and submits an expression of interest or investment instruction.
16. Funds move only through an approved payment/custody arrangement with clear status, receipts, reconciliation, and refund/withdrawal rules.
17. The farm submits scheduled progress reports against milestones; the platform records and makes approved reports visible to authorised investors.
18. Exceptions, delays, material changes, and complaints are escalated to the platform operations team.
5.3 Organisation collaborates on a project
19. Organisation submits a partnership or project enquiry.
20. Platform team qualifies the enquiry and arranges follow-up.
21. A project record is created with objectives, scope, geography, budget, beneficiaries, deliverables, milestones, owners, and reporting schedule.
22. Authorised parties receive project access and agree on roles and approvals.
23. Progress updates, field evidence, deliverables, risks, and expenses (where required) are submitted.
24. Project lead reviews and approves reports; stakeholders can view the latest approved status.
