11. Non-Functional Requirements
• Responsive design: usable on current desktop, tablet, and mobile browsers, including low-to-mid-range Android devices.
• Performance: aim for key public pages to load quickly on common Nigerian mobile networks; compress images and defer non-critical assets.
• Availability: define a target with the engineering team; proposed MVP target is 99.5% monthly uptime excluding planned maintenance.
• Security: HTTPS, secure password hashing, input validation, protection against common web vulnerabilities, rate limiting, secure file uploads, and least-privilege permissions.
• Privacy: collect only necessary personal data, explain its use, provide appropriate consent and retention controls, and restrict farm/investor documents.
• Reliability: daily backups at minimum, tested restoration procedures, monitoring, error logging, and documented incident response.
• Accessibility: readable typography, keyboard navigation for key flows, descriptive form labels, and adequate contrast.
• Maintainability: documented API contracts, database migrations, environment configuration, automated tests, and staging/production separation.
• Auditability: record who performed important administrative, approval, report, and financial actions.
• Scalability: architecture should support additional regions, user categories, agricultural sectors, and payment providers.
12. Suggested Technical Architecture
The engineering team may recommend alternatives, but the solution should include the following logical components:
• Frontend: responsive web application with accessible components and role-specific dashboards.
• Backend/API: secure application API with authentication, role-based access control, validation, business rules, and audit events.
• Database: relational database for users, farms, opportunities, service requests, projects, milestones, reports, and transactions.
• File storage: private object storage for identity/business documents, evidence, photos, and downloadable reports; signed or time-limited access links.
• Payment integration: provider integration with signed webhook verification, idempotent processing, reconciliation, and transaction logs.
• Notifications: email service first; optional SMS/WhatsApp integration after confirming consent, costs, and provider requirements.
• Administration: protected back-office interface with permissions and review queues.
• Monitoring: application logs, uptime monitoring, error alerts, backups, and security event tracking.
