18. Open Decisions for the Product Owner
• What is the organisation's official name, brand, logo, and domain?
• Will the platform charge subscription fees, listing fees, commissions, project-management fees, or a combination?
• Will the platform only introduce investors to farms, or will it actively facilitate investment transactions and disbursements?
• What investment models are intended: equity, debt/repayment, profit share, sponsorship, grants, or another structure? Each may require different legal treatment.
• Who will verify farms, professional credentials, and organisation legitimacy, and what evidence is required?
• Which payment provider and payout model will be used, and who is legally responsible for holding or transferring funds?
• What is the required reporting cadence (weekly, monthly, milestone-based) and who approves reports?
• Will users communicate through platform messaging, WhatsApp, email, or a combination?
• What languages are required at launch, and should the platform support low-bandwidth mode?
• What are the launch budget, timeline, hosting preference, support hours, and target number of initial users?
19. Final Product Principle
The platform must earn trust through verified identities and profiles, clear service terms, controlled opportunity publication, secure payment handling, transparent reporting, strong access controls, and honest communication about risk. Build the MVP around reliable workflows first, then expand based on validated user needs and legal/compliance readiness.

