22. Four Profile Types, Permissions, and Onboarding
22.1 Shared capabilities
• Secure sign-up/sign-in, email and/or phone verification, password reset, account recovery, consent capture, and session management.
• Profile with photo/logo, display name, biography, location, interests, goals, preferred agricultural sectors, and notification preferences.
• Personalised portal/feed containing eligible text, image, and video posts; search/filtering; reactions; comments; and conversations.
• Access to relevant live video events and recorded replays subject to event permissions, price/access rules, and recording consent.
• In-platform notifications for followed topics, replies, messages, events, jobs, payment status, and verification decisions.
• Privacy controls for profile fields, contact details, activity visibility, and communication preferences.
• Report/block/mute tools, community rules, support, and a way to appeal moderation decisions.
• Interests and goals used for feed ranking, event recommendations, job recommendations, and optional notification personalisation.
22.2 Profile A — Agriculture Enthusiast
Purpose: people who want to learn about agriculture, join discussions, attend events, and explore agricultural career opportunities.
• View and interact with text, photo, and video posts; comment, react, join discussion threads, and follow topics/creators.
• Join live video conferences/events and access eligible recordings from a searchable event library.
• Receive event reminders, live-now alerts, followed-topic updates, and replies to their activity.
• Set interests and goals such as poultry, crops, aquaculture, livestock, agribusiness, BSF/insect farming, careers, or other agricultural areas.
• Browse jobs, search/filter, save vacancies, view details, apply on-platform or follow an external application link, and track status when employers update it.
• Create a jobseeker profile with CV, skills, qualifications, experience, location/preferences, and a setting controlling employer visibility.
• Apply to become a creator. Publishing rights stay disabled until topic-specific screening is completed and an authorised reviewer approves the result.
• Screening may use a quiz, sample content, practical evidence, identity checks, or interview. Approval in one topic does not automatically approve all topics; retest/appeal options should be defined.
22.3 Profile B — Farmer / Farm
Purpose: farmers and farm entities seeking practical knowledge, advice, workers, and business connections.
• Use the shared feed, conversations, live events, replays, and notifications.
• Create a farm profile with farm type, location, scale/capacity, products, operational needs, and relevant verification documents.
• Discover consultants by specialisation, service area, language, availability, rate, experience, and verification status.
• Request/book paid consultations by audio or video call within the platform; see rate, duration, scope, and cancellation terms before confirming.
• Pay through an approved provider; receive booking confirmation/receipt and access booking history and dispute/support processes.
• Post job vacancies with title, duties, location, employment type, pay range where possible, required skills, closing date, and application method.
• Pay the listing fee or use an eligible package; see status, expiry, applications, and renewal/close controls.
• Maintain interests, goals, farm needs, and preferred consultant categories for recommendations.
22.4 Profile C — Agricultural Specialist / Consultant
Purpose: professionals and practitioners who provide expertise, publish educational material, offer paid consultations, and sell knowledge products.
• Use the shared feed, discussions, live/recorded events, and notifications.
• Complete a profile covering expertise categories, credentials, experience, service area, languages, portfolio, availability, and rates.
• Apply for creator status and pass topic-specific screening before publishing creator-gated educational content. Credential verification and creator screening are separate statuses.
• Publish approved text, image, and video content under moderation/community rules; content may be pre-reviewed or post-moderated.
• Offer paid consultations with configurable rates per hour or session, duration, available time slots, scope, and cancellation/no-show terms.
• Deliver consultations through secure platform audio/video integration. Record booking/session metadata; do not record call content by default.
• Publish books/digital learning products with title, author, description, cover, price, preview, format, access/download permissions, and refund terms.
• Create paid adverts for eligible services, products, or events using approved packages, campaign duration, and targeting where supported.
• View gross earnings, platform fees, refunds/chargebacks, pending and available balance, payout status/history, and statements.
• Receive eligible net earnings on a configured payout schedule after fees and permitted deductions, subject to verification, minimum thresholds, holds, disputes, and provider rules.
22.5 Profile D — Agricultural Business
Purpose: legitimate agricultural companies, cooperatives, suppliers, processors, service providers, input dealers, employers, and related organisations.
• Use the shared feed, discussions, live/recorded events, and notifications.
• Create a business profile with legal/trading name, category, address/region, authorised contact, website/social links, products/services, and verification evidence.
• Business verification must state what was checked and must not imply a blanket guarantee of quality, solvency, or performance.
• After verification and any required ad review, publish paid adverts and promote eligible products/services with descriptions, media, price or quote request, service area, availability, and enquiry route.
• Manage packages, campaign dates, invoices/receipts, performance metrics, enquiries/leads, renewals, and moderation decisions.
• Sponsor events through packages describing benefits, placement, duration, deliverables, price, and sponsorship terms.
• Post jobs under the employer workflow and manage applications where permitted.
• Only authorised business representatives can administer the profile, buy promotions, view leads, or access billing details.
