Mix text, image, and video posts from approved creators, followed accounts/topics, relevant businesses, events, and discussions. Role and visibility rules govern actions.
Feed controls
Pagination or efficient infinite scroll, search, topic/category filters, relevant sorting, and controls to mute/unfollow topics/accounts.
Interactions
Like/react, comment, reply in threads, follow creator, share within permitted platform surfaces, save/bookmark, and report.
Media
Validate types/sizes; generate thumbnails/transcode video as needed; secure storage; accessible captions/alt text support.
Content lifecycle
Draft, pending review, approved/published, changes requested, rejected, removed, appealed, archived; keep reviewer/timestamp audit history.
Recommendations
Use declared interests, follows, role, voluntarily provided location, and engagement; provide controls and do not expose private data.
Accessibility / low bandwidth
Responsive design, compressed media, captions/transcripts where available, keyboard navigation, readable text, and graceful weak-network handling.
 
All profile types can consume and interact with eligible content. Publishing rights depend on role, creator screening, business verification, moderation status, and fees. A verified business is not automatically an approved educational creator; a screened creator is not automatically a licensed professional.
24. Live Events, Video Conferences, and Replay Library
• Authorised users/admins can create events with title, description, topic, host/speakers, date/time/time zone, duration, audience, capacity, registration, price/access rules, and recording preference.
• Event directory/feed shows upcoming, live, completed, cancelled, and replay-available states.
• Users can register, receive confirmation/reminders, join through a supported browser, and receive live-now alerts when opted in.
• Integrate a video provider with suitable host/moderator controls, attendee management, chat/Q&A, and reporting.
• Publish approved recordings in a searchable library with title, topic, host/speaker, date, description, captions/transcript if available, and access controls.
• Disclose recording before/during the event and handle consent. Restrict recordings where content is paid, private, or sensitive.
• Organisers can review registration, attendance, engagement, sponsorship deliverables, and feedback where supported.
• Sponsorship must be clearly labelled and must not override safety, editorial, or community standards.
25. Agricultural Jobs Marketplace
25.1 Jobseeker experience
• Agriculture Enthusiasts can create a jobseeker profile, upload/update CV, add skills/qualifications/experience, set location/preferences, and control profile visibility.
• Job search/filter by keyword, specialisation, location, experience, employment type, remote/on-site, pay range if supplied, and closing date.
• Save vacancies, apply on-platform or use external application links, and view status where employers provide updates.
• Notify users about relevant vacancies and application status according to their preferences.
• Vacancy pages display employer identity/verification status, role requirements, location, pay information when supplied, closing date, and report-job option.
25.2 Employer / farm experience
• Farm/Farmer and verified Agricultural Business accounts can create/manage listings subject to role permissions and verification rules.
• Job form includes title, description, responsibilities, qualifications, employment type, location, pay range where available, number of openings, closing date, and application method.
• Screen for scams, discriminatory/prohibited content, misleading claims, and suspicious requests for payment.
• Listing states: Draft, Payment Pending, Under Review, Published, Paused, Expired, Rejected, Closed, Archived.
• Configure listing fees by duration, featured status, package/subscription, and approved options. Show price and refund/renewal rules before payment.
• Employers may access applicants and application materials only for their own vacancies and disclosed recruitment purposes.
• Candidates should not be charged simply to apply for an ordinary vacancy. Optional training/credential services must be separately described.
