27. Consultant Booking, Calls, Fees, and Earnings
• Consultant configures service category, rate, billing unit (per hour/session), minimum duration, available slots, service scope, and cancellation/no-show policy.
• Farmer selects consultant/service/time/duration; platform shows total price, fee treatment, and terms before checkout.
• Booking statuses include Requested/Checkout Started, Payment Pending, Confirmed, In Progress, Completed, Cancelled, No-show, Refunded, and Disputed as applicable.
• Audio/video call uses a secure provider integration. Capture booking/session metadata, not call content, unless recording is separately supported with consent and retention rules.
• After a completed consultation, farmer may submit a moderated rating/review.
• Consultant dashboard shows gross sale, platform commission, permitted provider charges, refunds/chargebacks, net payable, pending/available balance, payout date/status, and transaction reference.
28. Payments, Platform Fees, Ledger, and Scheduled Payouts
Maintain an auditable ledger and transparent fees. “Wallet” should initially mean an internal ledger of amounts due/earned, not an unlicensed deposit-taking or stored-value product. Use payment and payout providers appropriate to Nigerian law and provider rules.
28.1 Fee and ledger rules
• Admin can configure service commission, job fee, advert fee, book/product commission, event sponsorship fee, subscription price, and discounts by product type and effective date.
• Before checkout, show price, platform charge where applicable, provider/tax treatment where applicable, total payable, refund/cancellation terms, and seller/consultant net amount where relevant.
• Use immutable ledger entries for charge, platform fee, provider fee, refund, chargeback, adjustment, payout, reversal, and reconciliation. Do not rely only on a mutable balance field.
• Separate pending earnings from available earnings. Holds may apply for completion, refund windows, fraud review, chargeback exposure, compliance checks, or disputes under published terms.
• Payout eligibility requires verification, valid payout account, any configured minimum, no blocking hold, and reconciled transactions.
• Payout batches are configurable (e.g., weekly/monthly), previewable by authorised finance/admin, and traceable to included earnings and deductions.
• Use idempotency, provider references, payout status tracking, retry/failed-payout workflow, reconciliation, and support escalation.
• Notify consultants when earnings become available and when payouts are scheduled, processed, failed, held, or adjusted.
• Provide downloadable statements and audit fee-rule changes and payout decisions.
• Do not represent pending balances as bank deposits or guarantee a payout date when provider/compliance conditions can delay settlement.
