29. Books and Digital Learning Products
• Approved consultants/creators can submit title, author, topic, description, price, cover, sample/preview, format, language, publication date, and rights declaration.
• Authorised reviewers can approve, reject, suspend, or remove listings for copyright, quality, policy, or legal concerns.
• Purchasers view product details, pay, receive a receipt, and access content through secure account-linked library/download controls.
• Use reasonable access controls; download limits/watermarking are optional only if technically and legally appropriate.
• Provide refund/complaint handling, duplicate-purchase handling, and seller statements for gross sales, fees, refunds, and net earnings.
• Seller confirms distribution rights; provide a copyright complaint/takedown process.
30. Advertising, Business Listings, and Event Sponsorship
• Businesses and eligible consultants create adverts with format, headline, description, media, destination/contact action, target category/region where supported, schedule, package/budget, and terms.
• Clearly label sponsored placements as Sponsored/Advertisement and distinguish them from ordinary community posts.
• Admin controls categories, restricted/prohibited products, ad approval, suspension, refunds, reporting, and advertiser verification.
• Configure prices by placement, duration, format, region/audience, featured status, and sponsorship package. Show total before checkout.
• Campaign reporting may show measured impressions, clicks, enquiries/leads, registrations, and spend; do not promise outcomes or invent reach.
• Business profiles show products/services, description, enquiry route, location/service area, verification scope, campaigns, and terms.
• Event sponsorship packages specify logo/mentions, speaking opportunity if any, resource links, placement, audience exposure, dates, deliverables, reporting, cancellation, and any exclusivity.
