33. Admin and Operations Requirements
• Role-based admin console with separate permissions for support, content moderation, creator screening, business verification, jobs, ads, events, finance, and compliance.
• Review queues for creator applications, business verification, jobs, sponsored ads, books, reported content, payment exceptions, and payout batches.
• Admin manages topic taxonomy, profile options, listing duration/prices, commissions, minimum payout, payout schedule, promotions, and event access settings with audit logs.
• Support cases link to the relevant user, post, booking, job, purchase, payment, payout, or event.
• Financial history cannot be silently edited; corrections create auditable adjustment entries with reason and actor.
• Dashboards track signups, active users, reports, screening outcomes, event attendance, applications, bookings, transaction value, platform revenue, refunds, and payout exceptions.
34. Security, Privacy, Safety, and Compliance Additions
• Enforce server-side role-based access control for every API/data object; hiding frontend controls is not sufficient.
• Protect CVs, identity/business documents, consultation details, call links, purchased books, financial statements, and payout details with least-privilege access and time-limited links where appropriate.
• Obtain consent for event recording and disclose whether chat/attendee details may be recorded. Do not record private consultations by default.
• Use verified payment webhooks, idempotent processing, secure secret storage, reconciliation, rate limiting, fraud monitoring, and audit logs.
• Define retention/deletion rules for CVs, messages, recordings, payment records, verification documents, and assessment data; follow applicable Nigerian data-protection requirements and obtain legal review.
• Publish community standards, prohibited ad categories, job anti-scam policy, creator policy, advertiser terms, consultation cancellation/refund policy, digital product terms, and payout terms.
• Represent business verification, creator screening, and credential checks accurately and separately. Verification is not a guarantee of performance or advice outcomes.
• Review applicable Nigerian requirements for privacy/data protection, consumer protection, recruitment, tax, payments, digital content, advertising, and any retained investment features.
