36. Additional Acceptance Criteria
• A visitor can identify the four profile types and start the appropriate onboarding path from the landing page.
• Each profile sees the shared feed but only receives actions permitted by role, verification state, creator status, and content visibility.
• Users can save/update interests and goals and adjust notification preferences.
• An Agriculture Enthusiast can browse jobs, apply, and view their applications without paying to apply for an ordinary vacancy.
• A farmer can discover consultants, view rates/terms, book and pay for an audio/video consultation, and receive confirmation.
• A consultant cannot publish creator-gated content until topic-specific screening is approved; screening history is auditable.
• A consultant can list a book, receive approved purchases, and view gross sales, fees, refunds, and net earnings.
• A verified business can publish eligible paid adverts after required moderation/payment and submit event sponsorship requests.
• An employer/farm can pay for a listing, track approval/expiry, manage applications for its own vacancies, and close the job.
• A scheduled payout batch calculates earnings from ledger entries, applies configured charges, prevents duplicate payouts, and produces a reconciliation report.
• Admin can review creator applications, business verification, jobs, adverts, books, sponsorships, and reported content.
• Event attendees receive reminders; authorised users can join live events; permitted recordings can be published as replays.
• Users cannot access another user’s private CV, business documents, purchase entitlement, consultation link, transaction, or payout details without permission.
• Moderation, verification, fee-rule, payment, refund, and payout actions are audit logged.
• Core flows pass desktop/mobile, weak-network, failed-payment, and failed-payout tests.
37. Product Owner Decisions Required Before Development
• Confirm brand name, domain, launch regions/languages, and whether one user may operate multiple profile types.
• Approve release boundaries and priority order for feed, live video, jobs, consultant booking, digital books, adverts, and sponsorship.
• Choose live video/audio provider and confirm usage pricing, participant limits, recording, and integration requirements.
• Define creator screening by topic, assessors, pass thresholds, renewal/retest, and appeals.
• Define business verification evidence, reviewer, and exact meaning of the verified badge.
• Approve prices for job posts, consultant/business adverts, subscriptions, books, sponsorship, and consultation commissions.
• Approve commission rates, provider charges/taxes, refund rules, minimum payout, payout frequency, hold periods, and chargeback treatment.
• Select payment/payout providers and obtain advice on the legal structure for receiving, recording, and disbursing funds in Nigeria.
• Decide whether job applications are hosted on-platform or can link to external employer systems.
• Define moderation staffing/response times, prohibited categories, copyright complaints, event recording consent, and retention/deletion.
• Confirm whether original farm-investment functionality is included in launch or gated until legal/compliance approval.
• Confirm budget, launch date, expected user counts, service-level targets, and feature owners.
38. Revised Product Principle
The platform should function as a trusted agricultural ecosystem rather than a static directory. It combines useful education and community, verified expertise, transparent job and advertising listings, convenient consultations, valuable learning products, relevant events, and reliable payment/payout operations. Trust depends on clear permissions, truthful verification labels, moderation, transparent fees, secure handling of user and financial data, and honest reporting. Build in testable stages and do not activate regulated or high-risk financial flows before the necessary professional review and provider arrangements are complete.
